  "note": "[[monet|Monet]] painted the port of Le Havre from his hotel window in November 1872; an astronomer later used the sun and tides to pin it to 13 November, around 7:35 a.m. Shown in 1874, it gave [[impressionism|Impressionism]] its name. Neuroscientist Margaret Livingstone points out that the orange sun is about as light as the grey sky around it, a matter of [[value]]: in a black-and-white copy it nearly disappears."
